            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Gorsuch stated that the district\u2019s policies were neither neutral nor generally applicable."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The District cannot sustain its burden under any of the applicable tests."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas filed a concurring opinion agreeing that the district violated Kennedy\u2019s First Amendment rights."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "53dc3c56a3c6a70ddb15f2c727a2973a9e6567fd1880a62bda890046e30032a0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-53dc3c56a3c6-0004-0001"
